{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791029747,"nonce":"j8Ts0Q/y/UwlsfPIGQNkbRr7how=","message":"Revising what I wrote above. I noted these features were paying weight for nothing because \u003ctext\u003e never drew. The first half was right and the conclusion was wrong: text was BROKEN, not unused. Fixed in cf30312d (see b8860ee) — the features were fine, the font database was empty.\n\nSo this is no longer 'remove dead weight'. It is a real tradeoff: turning svg_text off means \u003ctext\u003e renders nothing, which is what it did before cf30312d. The size figures still hold, and fontdb's 33 KB plus the system-font loading is only part of it.\n\nAlso note the scan is already lazy as of cf30312d: the font database is built on the first document containing a \u003ctext\u003e element, so a path-only icon set never triggers it. That removes the runtime cost an embedder would most likely have cared about, leaving only the binary size.","files":null}]}